--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,19 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## API
+
+### `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`
+
+Returns the value of a JSON document that a JSON Pointer ([RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901))
+refers to. The empty pointer `""` returns the whole document; `~1` and `~0` escape `/` and `~`.
+
+- Throws `SyntaxError` when `pointer` is not a valid JSON Pointer (for example it does not start with `/`,
+  or contains a `~` not followed by `0` or `1`).
+- Throws `RangeError` when it does not resolve: a missing member, an out-of-range or non-canonical array
+  index (leading zeros, signs), the `-` token (the nonexistent element past the end of an array), or a step
+  into a string, number, boolean or `null`.
+- Only own members are read, so `__proto__` and `constructor` cannot reach the prototype chain. The document
+  is never mutated.
+- The URI fragment form of RFC 6901 section 6 (`#/foo`) is not supported.
